	<div class="entry-content clearfix">
					<a href="">
				<img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/createweb/Karwa-Chauth-Images/Karwa-Chauth-Mehndi.jpg" class="thumb alignleft" alt="Tradition of Heena" height="140" width="140" />			</a>
                   <p>
                 Mehandi Henna has its own significance in India and the Middle East. It's like a tradition in India, women use to adorn their hands and feet with henna mehndi. Mehandi Henna is basically a paste is made from henna leaves. Heena hs a special place for married women (suhagans) that normally apply in cases like this Karwa chauth.

Mehandi Henna is considered a symbol of good luck for married women in Indian culture. This is a belief in India that women with mehendi has left a dark color will have plenty of loving care of her husband.</p>
                    <p>
                 &nbsp;Heena and mehandi design are very beautiful and give beautiful looks to hands and feet of person.

The mehandi application activity is booming in the holiday season, especially at the time of Karwa chauth. At that time, most markets are full of people and goods. Henna artists create fascinating and complex patterns on the palms and feet of women is a common site in these markets. Mehendi salons offer makeup offers such exciting opportunities.
On every marriage, party  - women love to get Heena on their hand.

                    </p>
